{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning everyone. I'm Maj. Alvarez, the Battalion S-6. I'll be publishing the binding network access plan for tomorrow once the change-control board gets the service requirements from operations, logistics, and medical. To recap what we're working with: we have three network segments — Red, Blue, and Green — and three service windows: 0800-0900, 1000-1100, and 1400-1500. Each of the three services — the command video brief, the logistics synchronization feed, and the clinic records system — will get one segment and one window. I need each of you to provide your service requirements so we can finalize the plan. Also, keep in mind that each service must have a documented configuration control before its access window begins. What are your requirements?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Operations requirement: the command video brief must use Segment Green and the 1400-1500 window. The partner headquarters bridge is configured only for that segment and time. I received the bridge configuration confirmation this morning, but it's not yet on the change-control board slide."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Logistics requirement: the logistics synchronization feed must use Segment Blue and the 1000-1100 window. Its legacy terminal accepts only the Blue segment profile and the depot upload begins at 1000. I confirmed the terminal profile with the depot technician today, but this update has not been added to the network request yet."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Medical requirement: the clinic records system must use Segment Red and the 0800-0900 window. The clinic server's isolation certificate is valid only on Red, and the morning patient-file reconciliation starts at 0800. I received the certificate record from the clinic administrator this morning, but it has not been entered in the access worksheet yet."}
```

